# Multi-Tenant vs. Browser-Only: Architecture Decision

**Date:** 2026-08-20  
**Status:** DECIDED — defer to post-hackathon  
**Trigger:** Google login failure on venturebot.taskmind-ai.com raised the question of whether to add multi-tenant auth or remove server-side data entirely.

---

## The Problem

The current app stores user data (ideas, transcripts, PRDs, scores) in a server-side
SQLite database. This creates GDPR/data-protection exposure:

1. User data is stored on the server without consent management
2. No way for users to export or delete their data
3. No privacy policy, no terms of service
4. No user isolation (the DB is single-user by design, but multi-user would be exposed)

The Google SSO is also failing because the OAuth client ID's authorized origins
don't include the new domain.

## Options Considered

### Option A: Browser-only (IndexedDB)
- Remove all auth, SQLite, server-side persistence
- Backend becomes a pure stateless debate engine
- Frontend stores everything in IndexedDB
- **Pros:** Zero compliance exposure, no login, simpler architecture
- **Cons:** No cross-device, no crash recovery, no self-improvement across sessions, ephemeral data

### Option B: Multi-tenant backend
- Keep Google SSO, remove allowlist, add user_id scoping
- Add GDPR endpoints (export, delete)
- Add privacy policy, consent banner
- **Pros:** Full cross-device, self-improvement works, looks like a real product
- **Cons:** ~2-3 days engineering, ongoing legal exposure, compliance overhead

## Hackathon Context (Deadline: Aug 31, 2026)

The hackathon submission requirements are:
- **Demo video** (≤4 min, public YouTube) — primary evidence
- **URL to hosted project** — "highly encouraged" but not required
- **Code repository** (public or private)
- **README.md** with spin-up instructions
- **Judges are NOT required to test the live app** — they may judge solely on the video + text

The judging criteria for "Demo & Production Readiness" (30% weight) include:
- Clean architecture diagram
- Reproducible setup instructions
- Visual proof of GCP deployment in the video
- Unedited, live execution of the agent

**Key insight:** The video is what matters. The live URL is secondary. The current
working code (114 tests, full pipeline, dashboard, SSE, HITL gates) is the
strongest demo asset.

## Decision

**Defer the multi-tenant rearchitecture to post-hackathon.**

For the hackathon submission:
1. Fix the Google OAuth origin (add venturebot.taskmind-ai.com to the GCP console — 2 min)
2. Deploy the current app to Cloud Run (Dockerfile is ready)
3. Record the demo video with the current feature set
4. Submit to Devpost

## Post-Hackathon Plan

> Superseded by `PUBLIC_DEPLOYMENT_DESIGN.md` (2026-08-20) — the full
> queue/rate-limit/budget/BYOK/compliance design. This section is kept as
> the high-level decision summary.

### Phase 1: Legal & Compliance Agent
Add a new agent to the debate pipeline that checks:
- Data protection requirements for the proposed architecture
- Regulatory compliance (GDPR, CCPA, etc.)
- Whether the idea needs a "prototype mode" (no user data) or "production mode" (multi-tenant)

### Phase 2: Security Review Gate
Before implementation:
- Security audit of the proposed data model
- Input validation and rate limiting
- Anti-abuse measures (recaptcha, rate limiting, API key bring-your-own)

### Phase 3: Multi-Tenant Implementation
- User_id scoping on all DB tables
- Google SSO for any user (remove allowlist)
- GDPR endpoints: GET /api/user/data, DELETE /api/user/data
- Privacy policy, consent banner, cookie notice
- Session management with proper expiry

### Phase 4: "Prototype Mode" (alternative)
For ideas that don't need multi-tenant compliance:
- The compliance agent can flag "this can be a prototype"
- Prototype mode: no server-side data, browser-local only
- Production mode: full multi-tenant with compliance

